{"id": "EUVD-2026-108831", "enisaUuid": "776b6995-97b3-3de2-8a50-b83b54d3959c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm: fix reading free memory in do_resume\n\nWhen do_resume calls dm_table_get_mode(new_map), the call is done without\nholding any locks (it only holds a reference to the md). It may be\npossible that another concurrent ioctl on the same device will swap table\nafter dm_swap_table and before dm_table_get_mode. In this case,\ndm_table_get_mode(new_map) reads freed memory.\n\nThis race condition was triggered by syzbot.\n\nThis commit fixes the race by reading mode of the new table before\ndm_swap_table. Note that new_map is also passed to dm_ima_need_measure,\nbut this function doesn't attempt to dereference it, so this call should\nbe safe.\n\nNote that this is not a security bug because only root can trigger it and\nthe commonly used tools such as lvm or cryptsetup do not call the ioctls\nconcurrently, so that they can't trigger it acceidentally.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:21:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:21:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/281f68d6cf8acb2547ebf0a849b8beae8fb0ec3c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c96d1a8324e7736e0f8a5790ecf39d36c2c4a82", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3bf232c913b7e0103d323f15e6342d37cb1b357", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/301691c32b8ad023e3316d5dbb6a8cf52d47b0dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9417c1c5269e2bd0570fbe53e4ec03a8d31f008"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99036"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cdcd69b-d650-34f0-bfaa-d59168a359cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.113"}, {"id": "1cf19a02-8c3f-31cb-a877-9524a7fbb530", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "24d0a30b-da5b-309c-a9da-5bb47f6ccc27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2feb673a-c257-3579-8c67-2417b7d8292f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <e3bf232c913b7e0103d323f15e6342d37cb1b357"}, {"id": "4510872b-e2c4-3c9c-9d1d-693ead7c7c5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "5a8106f9-9bf7-3fa3-ac09-40d0ebef7040", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <281f68d6cf8acb2547ebf0a849b8beae8fb0ec3c"}, {"id": "70b57473-29fd-342f-9182-775798ab4b7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <7.2.11"}, {"id": "928acad4-1d6c-3ef3-899b-e16e2e783fb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.18.57"}, {"id": "9752c800-b661-3c40-bb17-4f69a273f8e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "a44a6809-0700-3654-98a4-00857b48083f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <2c96d1a8324e7736e0f8a5790ecf39d36c2c4a82"}, {"id": "bb3a7a78-1050-3ba9-84d5-fe80ca9dc395", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <301691c32b8ad023e3316d5dbb6a8cf52d47b0dc"}, {"id": "bf664189-e846-30a7-b48b-d8b43c97c1ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c9417c1c5269e2bd0570fbe53e4ec03a8d31f008"}, {"id": "ce0e7fd4-aaa5-3eda-b2ec-2dac6091f60d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e2eb5128-981b-35b6-8fef-451b6534d035", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2f0301b3-5b7b-3b18-9cdf-a51f4434